{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":70,"recorded_at":1780531400000135,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ca08-9953-7f32-a957-4b38ff21f0e0"},"task_id":"01a0ca08-9953-7f32-a957-4b38ff21f0e0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ca08-9953-7f32-a957-4b38ff21f0e0","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-3-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-1c28dz/; echo \\\"===\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-1c28dz/TASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr9.md 2>/dev/null | head -100\",\n  \"description\": \"List resources and read reviewer cr9\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"TASK-260830-1c28dz_producer.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr1.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr2.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr3.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr4.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr5.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr6.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr7.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr8.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_reviewer-cr9.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev10.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev2.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev3.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev4.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev5.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev6.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev7.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev8.md\\nTASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev9.md\\n===\\nIndependently review Change Request revision 9 of TASK-260830-1c28dz (implement-tmux-lifecycle-operations), the SECOND of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend). The chain is 35urbp -> 1c28dz -> g0pcnt; 35urbp (private tmux server management) is the signed checkpoint `1ba06e9` on the Story branch and g0pcnt carries the registry. Change Request shape: task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 40bb8c9; checkpointed predecessors d4bd91d ; tip d4bd91d0e740285b21b8d65bf6f074c8009b04ae), published by RUN-260922-97159f on muse-spark max, 49 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-1c28dz_change-request_rev9.patch / _rev9-validation.log. Revisions 1..8 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 9 on its own merits.. Read the producer brief TASK-260830-1c28dz_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-1c28dz_results.md, TASK-260830-1c28dz_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-1c28dz_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the predecessor's accepted evidence (TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md and its verdict TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev7.md), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes.\\n\\nNORMATIVE AUTHORITY: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` **§4.2** (1403-1449, including the five-step after-restore sequence at 1433-1441) and **§3.2** (806-813: the runtime root, the socket path `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock`, and component-by-component custody without following a symlink), with **§4.C** (1082), **§4.D** (1220), **§4.E** (1309) and **§4.4** (1478-1490) as context. The task record still names v0.5.0 and that is stale — a candidate citing a v0.5.0 line number or quoting text absent from the pinned file is a finding. Derive every expectation from the spec text, never from a production constant.\\n\\nREVISION HISTORY: every earlier revision of this leaf was routed CHANGES REQUESTED. Their verdicts are attached as `TASK-260830-1c28dz_review-verdict-rev<N>.md` for every N below the revision you are reviewing, and the rework brief that answered each is attached as `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-rev<N>.md`. Read the verdict immediately before yours and the brief that answered it before grading anything as closed or recurring, and use `repeat-of:` when a finding is the same class at an adjacent site. Where this brief and an attached verdict disagree, the verdict is authoritative.\\n\\nVerify with your own instruments, on isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree; never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration. Another Story is producing concurrently on this host, so record wall-clock and load for any gate you time.\\n\\n(1) **Eight operations, eight witnesses.** Create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore. Check each is driven through a production entry by a named committed test and that the results state the n-of-8 ratio with a call site per operation. One operation's test standing in for another's is a finding; so is an operation reported as driven whose test reaches only a helper.\\n\\n(2) **The after-restore sequence is ordered, and its order is the property.** §4.2 1433-1441: read the latest locally known lease; attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever; resume locally ONLY under a winning local lease with valid materialization; offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an interactive terminal; otherwise enter `parked` WITHOUT launching the provider. Drive each branch and assert the outcome. Plant a reordering — an earlier step's refusal swallowing a later step's offer is exactly the defect a sibling Story shipped and had to repair, so check that the offer branch is reachable under a lapsed local grant, and that \\\"without blocking forever\\\" has a measured bound rather than a sentence.\\n\\n(3) **The four handovers from the first leaf.** That leaf shipped the decision core and argv only and named this leaf as owner for: the exec and probe adapters (its `Dependencies` had NO production implementation — verify they exist now and are driven, and that the server socket carries crash and idempotency evidence or an explicit purity bound); **B18** the `sun_path` limit (104 bytes on macOS) against the derived socket path; **B16** an `ax` invocation from inside its own AX pane refusing `ambient collision`; and **B19/B20** the SPEC 810-812 before-bind rejection of a socket path, parent or ancestor with unsafe ownership or permissions — a 0777 root is admitted today on every first-leaf entry, so check whether this leaf's bind step rejects it or states why not. Grade each as closed with its test, deferred with reason and owner, or silently dropped.\\n\\n(4) **The census is a deliverable, and its asymmetry is where to attack.** Verify the gate × entry census exists, that its counts reproduce mechanically, and that its per-entry kill attribution holds for the cells marked Measured. Then pick a gate it marks Measured at one entry and plant a narrowing at a DIFFERENT entry that reaches the same gate. Check the two-sided-gate symmetry lines: the predecessor's last P2 was a gate whose two sides carried different row counts, and its own census displayed the asymmetry without flagging it. A cell reading \\\"pinned at the helper\\\" and nothing else is the hole that cost that leaf six rounds.\\n\\n(5) **Determinism, verified not read.** Every rule must be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere; any real-tmux test must be separately gated and never the only witness for an acceptance row. Verify by running the suite in an environment where the tmux binary cannot be resolved, and report exactly which tests fail or skip — a row whose only witness skips there is unmeasured however green the producer's log looks. Check the converse too: a rule degraded into a mock-only shape so it could be tested is a finding, not a solution; the production entry must still be the thing under test.\\n\\n(6) **No forked owners, and composition proven by driving.** `internal/tmuxserver` (the predecessor), `internal/terminalbackend`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/secprim`, `internal/localstore`, `internal/fencing`, `internal/sessstate` are landed. Grep for a second model of anything they own. The results must name which existing type or gate was extended and which deliberately was not — verify that claim rather than accepting it. Then take outcome grids (not name-keyed per-test lists) over the complete importer set on the CR base and on the candidate and diff them; every class that moved must be named in the results with its before and after. If a landed test was changed to accept new behaviour, grade the argument and its spec citation — a landed regression test rewritten without one is a P1.\\n\\n(7) **Traceability boundary.** This leaf must NOT touch `internal/traceability` (registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) — that belongs to g0pcnt. Any edit there is a finding. A package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix are the right places.\\n\\n(8) **Mutation and hygiene.** Rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowings of your own on gates the producer did not mutate, plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators, NOT_APPLIED is not a pass. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or your copies. gofmt/vet clean including `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` — the predecessor lost a round to a test file that reassigned a unix-only seam with no build constraint, and the local suite's `GOOS=windows go build` compiles no test files, so construction being green proves nothing there. The candidate byte-identical to trunk outside this Story's scope: check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> <current origin/main>` that also appears in the candidate, because a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies that read as reverts, and `task-board.config.json` must equal the base byte-for-byte. The full configured suite green on the exact tree; read the command count from the candidate config.\\n\\nReport the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-1c28dz_review-verdict-rev9.md and TASK-260830-1c28dz_review-evidence-rev9.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then `accept_cr(TASK-260830-1c28dz, revision=9, evidence=TASK-260830-1c28dz_review-verdict-rev9.md)` or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \\\"Rework scope (for the producer)\\\" section at the end. Model: gpt-6-astra low. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9676,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2419,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
