{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":468,"recorded_at":1780531400000931,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"call_id":"call_01a0ca098acb7683bc368463c80a8fe1","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1c28dz/TASK-260830-1c28dz_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-1c28dz rev9 results — implement-tmux-lifecycle-operations\n2|\n3|Revision 9 closes all five verdict-rev8 findings: one P1 fail-open\n4|boundary (peer-census directory skip), three P2 behavior gaps (stop\n5|poll in-flight bound, same-client replay with a peer present, kill\n6|attribution), and the evidence-freshness process failure. The\n7|candidate is UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree against checkpoint\n8|`d4bd91d0`.\n9|\n10|## 1. Finding dispositions\n11|\n12|| Finding | Severity | Disposition | Evidence |\n13||---|---|---|---|\n14|| P1 receipt-namespace directory skipped | P1 | FIXED: `Peers` skips only staging (`attach-*`) and non-receipt names; a directory at a receipt-shaped name errors, and the attach refuses with no receipt, no argv, no authorized input | `TestAttachPeerDirectoryFailsClosed` (entry, two legs) + `TestAttachStorePeersDirectoryFailsClosed` (census); narrowings `N-attach-peers-dir-skip` (tmuxserver, cross-package plant) and `N-attach-peers-dir` (termbind), both KILLED |\n15|| P2-A stop poll waits past the deadline | P2 | FIXED: one shared `probeContext` bounds the stop poll, the terminate-stale self-confirm, and the status live probes in-flight; expiry concludes unknown, never a verdict | `TestExecuteStopPollHonorsOperationDeadline`, `TestExecuteTerminateConfirmHonorsOperationDeadline`, `TestExecuteStatusProbeHonorsOperationDeadline` (release-controlled, refusal-before-release); shared narrowing `N-probe-deadline` KILLED through each entry alone; runner audit in §2 |\n16|| P2-B same-client replay refused with a peer present | P2 | FIXED: a Lookup-proven recorded receipt exempts the identical retry (replay, or `idempotency_mismatch` when transport/input changed); a client with no recorded receipt still gates | `TestAttachSameClientRetryWithPeerPresent` (input + read-only + conflict legs); narrowing `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` KILLED |\n17|| P2-C stale evidence archive | P2 | FIXED: the rev9 archive is built from the frozen rev9 tree, attached by absolute path, read back, and digest-verified | `TASK-260830-1c28dz_producer-evidence-rev9.tar.gz`, sha256 recorded in §9 and verified after attach |\n18|| P2-D overstated kill attribution | P2 | FIXED: fixtures drive the admitted class (30-min-past expiry, on-deadline instant leg, 6.5h advance with release-controlled barrier); every shared plant kills through every claimed killer ALONE, twice | Isolated logs `isolated/round{1,2}/<plant>.<test>.log` in the tarball; per-test table in §4 |\n19|\n20|## 2. Runner-wait audit (P2-A)\n21|\n22|Every `Runner.Run` call site in the leaf, dispositioned through the\n23|same shared contract (a read-only wait/probe carries a\n24|deadline-derived context; expiry concludes unknown, never a\n25|verdict):\n26|\n27|| Site | Class | Disposition |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| `backend.go` `pollSession` has-session (stop pre/post poll, terminate tail) | read-only poll | BOUNDED by the graceful/op deadline via `probeContext`; answered probes follow the clock exactly, only never-answered probes conclude by the context. Test + shared row (§1) |\n30|| `backend.go` `terminateStale` confirm has-session | read-only probe | BOUNDED by the op deadline via `probeContext`; expiry maps to the existing unknown arm. Test + shared row (§1) |\n31|| `status.go` `ObserveStatus` list-panes / list-sessions | read-only probes | BOUNDED by the query deadline via `probeContext`; expiry surfaces the existing uncoded-unknown mapping, never absent. Test + shared row (§1) |\n32|| `backend.go` `observeBoundary` wait-for | blocking wait | Already bounded (wait context); unchanged |\n33|| `boundaryProviderRows` list-panes | read-only probe | Already bounded (runs under the wait context); unchanged |\n34|| `ServerAdmission` / barrier acquire | blocking waits | Already bounded (uniform wait contract, rev8); unchanged |\n35|| `UnixDialer` dial | blocking dial | Already bounded (1s timeout); unchanged |\n36|| `closeInput` lock/detach, `execEvidence` send-keys/new-session, escalation kill, terminate kill | single-shot commits | Caller-cancellation-bounded; stated bound B45 (mid-commit cancellation cannot un-commit; the landed engine passes its context through to commits and checks the deadline between effects; this leaf mirrors that contract; a hung commit hangs, never mis-verdicts). Owner: this leaf for the audit; `internal/terminstance` for any engine-wide change |\n37|| `ServerSpawner.Spawn` (bind step, `context.Background`) | commit on the acquire path | Caller-cancellation does not reach it (the landed `Dependencies.Spawn` signature takes no context); stated bound B45 with the interface change owned by TASK-260830-35urbp. Hang-only, never a wrong verdict |\n38|\n39|## 3. New tests and narrowings\n40|\n41|Production call sites: `Peers` (`internal/termbind/overlap.go`),\n42|`checkAttachOverlap` (`internal/tmuxserver/ops.go`),\n43|`probeContext` + `pollSession` + `terminateStale`\n44|(`internal/tmuxserver/backend.go`), `ObserveStatus`\n45|(`internal/tmuxserver/status.go`).\n46|\n47|| Test (all through `Lifecycle.Execute` unless noted) | Finding | Narrowing | Verdict |\n48||---|---|---|---|\n49|| `TestAttachPeerDirectoryFailsClosed` (refuse-dir + still-skipped legs) | P1 | `N-attach-peers-dir-skip` | KILLED |\n50|| `TestAttachStorePeersDirectoryFailsClosed` (termbind census direct) | P1 | `N-attach-peers-dir` | KILLED |\n51|| `TestExecuteStopPollHonorsOperationDeadline` | P2-A | `N-probe-deadline` (shared) | KILLED alone |\n52|| `TestExecuteTerminateConfirmHonorsOperationDeadline` | P2-A | `N-probe-deadline` (shared) | KILLED alone |\n53|| `TestExecuteStatusProbeHonorsOperationDeadline` | P2-A | `N-probe-deadline` (shared) | KILLED alone |\n54|| `TestAttachSameClientRetryWithPeerPresent` (input + readonly + conflict) | P2-B | `N-attach-overlap-replay-unproven` | KILLED |\n55|| `TestExecuteQuiesceRefusesStaleFactsBetweenCommands` (repaired: 13:30 expiry + deadline-instant leg) | P2-D | `N-stop-escalation-expiry`, `N-stop-escalation-deadline` | KILLED alone (each) |\n56|| `TestBoundaryCommitWaitBoundedByOperationDeadline` (repaired: 6.5h + release) | P2-D | `N-attach-wait-deadline` | KILLED alone |\n57|\n58|No `tmux` process anywhere in any test (fake runners + a\n59|context-honoring blocking runner); zero real-tmux witnesses by the\n60|determinism design (bound B1, carried).\n61|\n62|## 4. Isolated kill attribution (P2-D)\n63|\n64|Each shared plant applied once, each claimed killer run ALONE\n65|(anchored `-run`), two rounds. Raw logs:\n66|`isolated/round{1,2}/<plant>.<test>.log`.\n67|\n68|| Plant | Killer alone | Round 1 | Round 2 | Precision in the same run |\n69||---|---|---|---|---|\n70|| `N-stop-escalation-generation` | stop stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | other-fact subtests green |\n71|| `N-stop-escalation-generation` | quiesce stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | other-fact subtests green |\n72|| `N-stop-escalation-expiry` | stop stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | other-fact subtests green |\n73|| `N-stop-escalation-expiry` | quiesce stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | authorization subtest reddens, generation/deadline green |\n74|| `N-stop-escalation-deadline` | stop stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | deadline-instant reddens, strictly-past green |\n75|| `N-stop-escalation-deadline` | quiesce stale-facts | KILLED | KILLED | deadline-instant reddens, strictly-past green |\n76|| `N-attach-wait-deadline` | attach wait | KILLED | KILLED | admission + barrier subtests both redden |\n77|| `N-attach-wait-deadline` | quiesce-span wait | KILLED | KILLED | single test |\n78|| `N-attach-wait-deadline` | boundary-commit wait | KILLED | KILLED | admitted wait commits, timeout assertion reddens |\n79|| `N-attach-wait-deadline` | attach cancel (companion) | GREEN | GREEN | cancellation unaffected by the widening |\n80|| `N-probe-deadline` | stop poll deadline | KILLED | KILLED | verdict lands at the release, not the bound |\n81|| `N-probe-deadline` | terminate confirm deadline | KILLED | KILLED | verdict lands at the release, not the bound |\n82|| `N-probe-deadline` | status probe deadline | KILLED | KILLED | verdict lands at the release, not the bound |\n83|\n84|Effect-recheck symmetry is now measured stop 4 / quiesce 4 (3\n85|shared arms × 2 entries above, plus the two single-killer skip\n86|rows); the wait bound kills through all 4 wait paths (attach\n87|admission, attach barrier, quiesce span, boundary commit).\n88|\n89|## 5. Census and battery\n90|\n91|- Table D: 148 gates × 21 entries = 3108 cells; 206 M / 186 B /\n92|  2716 U, verified by script over the table (`count_census.py` in\n93|  the tarball). New rows: `peershape`, `overlapreplay`,\n94|  `confirmbound`, `statusbound`; `pollbound` moves from B29 to\n95|  measured, with the terminate tail corrected from U1 to B39\n96|  (terminate-stale effects include `process_closed`, so the tail\n97|  reaches the shared poll; measured at EXE).\n98|- Table C recounted from the Table D gate set: 148 × 11 = 1628\n99|  cells (1610 U2a + 18 U2c).\n100|- Totals: 266 measured of 5504 (50+10+206 M across Tables\n101|  A/B/D); 190 bound; 5048 unreachable with reasons. Bound-cell\n102|  split verified by ID: 27 driven-but-rowless\n103|  (B22/B23/B32/B36) + 159 named undriven gaps\n104|  (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 + 152 B39).\n105|- Battery: 296/296 tmuxserver rows as expected (289 narrowing\n106|  KILLED + 5 supplementary KILLED + 1 shadowed SURVIVED + 1\n107|  control SURVIVED) on two full passes with one raw log per\n108|  plant per pass; 42/42 termbind rows as expected (40 narrowing\n109|  KILLED + 1 supplementary + 1 control) on two full verbose\n110|  passes. Combined 338/338.\n111|- Bounds: B29 revised to the exact-instant remainder (non-cell);\n112|  B44 clarified (receipt-validated replay here, liveness with\n113|  TASK-260922-vcx6yo); B45 stated (commits bounded by caller\n114|  cancellation). The conformance matrix mirrors Table B/D\n115|  byte-identically, AC rows 59-92 in both copies, and bounds\n116|  B22-B45 (mirror check in the tarball).\n117|\n118|## 6. Operation coverage (8 of 8)\n119|\n120|Each operation driven through `Lifecycle.Execute` by a named\n121|committed test (call site `Execute`, `lifecycle.go`):\n122|\n123|| Operation | Witness | Second witness (rev9) |\n124||---|---|---|\n125|| create | `TestExecuteCreateInteractive` | — |\n126|| attach | `TestExecuteAttach` | `TestAttachSameClientRetryWithPeerPresent`, `TestAttachPeerDirectoryFailsClosed` |\n127|| status | `TestExecuteStatusPresent` | `TestExecuteStatusProbeHonorsOperationDeadline` |\n128|| quiesce | `TestExecuteQuiesce` | — (repaired stale-facts legs) |\n129|| safe-boundary | `TestExecuteBoundary` | — (repaired commit-wait fixture) |\n130|| stop | `TestExecuteStop` | `TestExecuteStopPollHonorsOperationDeadline` |\n131|| stale termination | `TestExecuteTerminate` | `TestExecuteTerminateConfirmHonorsOperationDeadline` |\n132|| restore | `TestExecuteRestore` | — |\n133|\n134|## 7. Composition (base vs candidate)\n135|\n136|Base is the pristine checkpoint tree (`git archive d4bd91d0`);\n137|candidate is the frozen rev9 worktree. Both comparisons are\n138|outcome-keyed over the complete importer set (the whole-repo\n139|suite is a superset of every importer; the entry corpus covers\n140|the direct composition surface).\n141|\n