{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cad3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":964,"recorded_at":1780531400001923,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ca0b-fe7d-7d51-a4d8-cef36f0fd8b3"},"task_id":"01a0ca0b-fe7d-7d51-a4d8-cef36f0fd8b3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ca0b-fe7d-7d51-a4d8-cef36f0fd8b3","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-32-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n -B2 -A15 \\\"closure\\\" /tmp/rev5ev/evidence-rev5/results-rev5.md | head -80\",\n  \"description\": \"Read rev5 closure definition\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"18-## P1-A — the barrier verdict is the incarnation-scoped proof alone\\n19-\\n20:Construction: every closure report binds the incarnation that was\\n21-current when it recorded; a fresh create or restore success rotates\\n22-the incarnation to its own idempotency key; replays never rotate;\\n23-the attach entry consults exactly `QuiesceBarrierProven` (plus a\\n24-store-health read whose value is ignored and whose error fails\\n25-closed). Advisory memory, caller-carried source state, and failure\\n26-reporting cannot reopen a closed barrier because admission never\\n27-reads their values; a new incarnation supersedes stale reports\\n28-because the scan skips them. Row 79's lost-write claim now reads\\n29-as the construction (memory is advisory; the proof decides).\\n30-\\n31-Writer census — every writer of barrier-relevant state:\\n32-\\n33-| # | Writer (file:function) | What it writes | Proof the barrier holds |\\n34-|---|---|---|---|\\n35-| W1 | lifecycle.go:executeCreate success | best-effort Active/Parked memory; checked incarnation rotation on fresh success only | `TestExecuteCreateReplayPreservesBarrier` (replay skips) + `TestExecuteCreateIncarnationWriteFailureFailsClosed` (lost rotation fails closed); memory values proven ignored by `TestExecuteAdvisoryMemoryNeverDecidesAdmission` |\\n36-| W2 | lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp non-barrier success | best-effort memory (stop) | `TestExecuteStop` memory pin; values ignored for admission (same advisory test) |\\n37:| W3 | lifecycle.go:executeEngineOp barrier success | checked memory (status fidelity) + closure report binding the current incarnation | `TestExecuteAttachRefusesInputWhenQuiescing` + `N-quiesce-state-record` / `N-boundary-state-record` |\\n38-| W4 | lifecycle.go:recordFailure | first echo only when absent; honest unknown overwrites | `TestReviewFailedStopCannotEraseQuiescence` + `N-failure-preserves-record` (never-overwrite); `TestExecuteTerminateResumesAfterEffectFailure` (first-echo resume) |\\n39-| W5 | ops.go:executeAttach success | best-effort active memory | `TestExecuteAttach` memory pin; values ignored for admission (same advisory test) |\\n40-| W6 | ops.go:runLifecycleEffects success | best-effort target memory; checked incarnation rotation on fresh restore only | `TestExecuteRestoreReplayPreservesBarrier` + `D-restore-replay-rotation` (structural, B41); `TestExecuteTerminate` + `N-terminate-no-rotation` (terminate never rotates) |\\n41:| W7 | state.go:RecordOutcome via report funcs | closure report + incarnation bind, first success records, retries replay | `TestExecuteQuiesceRetryAfterStateWriteFailureHealsBarrier` (+ boundary twin); `N-quiesce-report-record` / `N-boundary-report-record` |\\n42-\\n43-Reader census — every reader deciding admission:\\n44-\\n45-| # | Reader (file:function) | What it trusts | Proof / bound |\\n46-|---|---|---|---|\\n47:| R1 | ops.go:checkAttachQuiesced | the incarnation-scoped closure proof as the sole verdict | `TestExecuteAdvisoryMemoryNeverDecidesAdmission` forces memory both directions with no verdict change; `N-quiesce-attach-gate` (re-anchored to the proof) |\\n48-| R2 | ops.go:checkAttachQuiesced health read | nothing (value ignored); read errors propagate | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnStateReadFailure` + `N-attach-health-check`; the Lookup absent arm itself is `N-state-read-absent` |\\n49-| R3 | state.go:QuiesceBarrierProven scoping | current incarnation; stale reports skipped | `TestExecuteQuiesceStopRestoreReopensBarrier` + `N-attach-barrier-incarnation`; store-level `TestQuiesceBarrierIgnoresSupersededIncarnation` |\\n50-| R4 | status.go:ClassifyStatus memory leg | advisory memory for status only, never admission | status rows 80/88; the reopen test admits attach while stale reports persist, proving the split |\\n51-\\n52-The two reviewer sequences run verbatim:\\n53-`TestReviewExistingActiveMemoryCannotReopenQuiescedInput` (stale\\n54-active + lost state write refuses via the proof) and\\n55-`TestReviewFailedStopCannotEraseQuiescence` (failed stop preserves\\n56-quiescing memory and refuses). The legitimate reopening is\\n57-`TestExecuteQuiesceStopRestoreReopensBarrier` (quiesce→stop→\\n58-restore→writable attach admitted, incarnation asserted).\\n59-\\n60-Bound B40 (owner: axpane receipt/bootstrap contracts): a lost\\n61:rotation with a prior closure stays closed with no\\n62-production-entry recovery — retries replay without rotating, and a\\n63-fresh key is unreachable (one bootstrap per session, pinned\\n64-mechanically in\\n65-`TestExecuteCreateIncarnationWriteFailureFailsClosed` via the\\n66-landed `idempotency_mismatch`). Over-strict in the safe direction;\\n67:a lost rotation with no prior closure is harmless (self-consistent\\n68-zero incarnation). Bound B41 (owner: this leaf): the restore\\n69-replay skip is structural (no code to narrow); the supplementary\\n70-`D-restore-replay-rotation` proves the test observes the forbidden\\n71-write.\\n72-\\n73-## P1-B — one composed authorization over six members\\n74-\\n75-`checkRestoreComposedBound` (wrapper.go) refuses\\n76-`local_precondition_failed` before any effect unless the executed\\n77-restore names the decided session, bootstrap, admitted-descriptor\\n78-instance/backend/generation triple, and winner lease/epoch. The\\n79-descriptor triple comes from the landed\\n80-`terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` output inside Decide —\\n81-compared, never re-parsed.\\n82-\\n--\\n114-| R4 EISDIR state-read failure | `TestExecuteAttachErrorsOnStateReadFailure` via `Execute(attach)` | `N-state-read-absent` — admits exactly EISDIR as absence |\\n115-\\n116:## P2-A — closure outcome grid (36-package variant, declared)\\n117-\\n118:The fixed-corpus driver `closuregrid` (ships in the evidence\\n119-tarball, copied into each tree; no clock, no randomness, no\\n120-network; filesystem probes normalized to `<tmp>`) records\\n121-`(package, entry, input class) -> (outcome, refusal string,\\n122:value summary)` over the reviewer's 36-package closure\\n123-(34 production + crashgate + environ). 33 packages probed;\\n124-3 stated bounds with owners (no exported pure callable\\n125-surface; fenced by the suite-verdict grid below): cloneproject,\\n126-crashgate, sshtransport. The 7 tmuxserver records for\\n127:story-added entries sit behind the `closuregrid_candidate`\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6208,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1552,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
