{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cbef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":1106,"recorded_at":1780531400002207,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ca0d-55cd-7351-9b5c-cbd02bd680fb"},"task_id":"01a0ca0d-55cd-7351-9b5c-cbd02bd680fb","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ca0d-55cd-7351-9b5c-cbd02bd680fb","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree/internal/termbind/mutant_harness.py`.\n(439 line(s) above)\n440|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/successor.go\",\n441|        find='\\t\\t\"supersedes_binding_id\":  prior.BindingID,\\n',\n442|        replace='\\t\\t\"supersedes_binding_id\":  nil,\\n',\n443|        count=1,\n444|        run=\"TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations\",\n445|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n446|        note=\"Admits exactly the linkless successor past the supersedes arm (the link is a singleton presence: nil vs set, and the prior pins nil). Kill path: the minted successor omits its prior link.\",\n447|    ),\n448|    Mutant(\n449|        name=\"N-successor-identity-field\",\n450|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/successor.go\",\n451|        find='\\tidentity, err := bindingIdentity(staged, \"binding_id\")\\n',\n452|        replace='\\tidentity, err := bindingIdentity(staged, \"session_id\")\\n',\n453|        count=1,\n454|        run=\"(TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations|TestMintSuccessorBindingIdentityBinds)\",\n455|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n456|        note=\"Admits exactly the wrong omit-field past the identity arm; the tampered-rebound parse still refuses. Kill path: the minted identity fails its own re-admission self-check.\",\n457|    ),\n458|    Mutant(\n459|        name=\"N-successor-generation-inherit\",\n460|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/successor.go\",\n461|        find='\\t\\t\"backend_generation\":     generation,\\n',\n462|        replace='\\t\\t\"backend_generation\":     prior.BackendGeneration,\\n',\n463|        count=1,\n464|        run=\"(TestMintSuccessorBindingSuccessesAcrossGenerations|TestMintSuccessorBindingRefusesSameGeneration)\",\n465|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n466|        note=\"Admits exactly the stale generation into the successor body; the succession-contradiction arm still compares the parameter. Kill path: the minted successor names the prior generation.\",\n467|    ),\n468|    Mutant(\n469|        name=\"N-attach-peers-decode\",\n470|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/overlap.go\",\n471|        find='\\t\\treceipt, err := decodeAttachReceipt(raw)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, err\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n472|        replace='\\t\\treceipt, err := decodeAttachReceipt(raw)\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n473|        count=1,\n474|        run=\"TestAttachStorePeersFailsClosed\",\n475|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n476|        note=\"Admits exactly the undecodable peer past the census health arm as a skip (the corrupt receipt reads as no peer); every other census failure still errors. Kill path: the peer scan passes over the corrupt document instead of refusing the census.\",\n477|    ),\n478|    Mutant(\n479|        name=\"N-attach-peers-dir\",\n480|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/overlap.go\",\n481|        find='\\t\\tif entry.IsDir() {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"attach peer %q is not a receipt file\", name)\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n482|        replace='\\t\\tif entry.IsDir() {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n',\n483|        count=1,\n484|        run=\"TestAttachStorePeersDirectoryFailsClosed\",\n485|        expect=\"KILLED\",\n486|        note=\"Admits exactly receipt-namespace directories past the census shape arm as skips (a directory at a receipt name reads as no peer); undecodable files and foreign receipts still error, staging and non-receipt entries still skip. Kill path: the peer scan passes over the receipt directory instead of refusing the census.\",\n487|    ),\n488|    Mutant(\n489|        name=\"C-control\",\n490|        path=f\"{PACKAGE}/doc.go\",\n491|        find=\"// Division of authority (composed, never forked): v4 payload construction\\n\",\n492|        replace=\"// Division of authority (composed, never forked; control): v4 payload construction\\n\",\n493|        count=1,\n494|        run=\"TestCheckInstanceIdentityAdmitsUUIDv7\",\n495|        expect=\"SURVIVED\",\n496|        note=\"Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive.\",\n497|    ),\n498|]\n499|\n500|\n501|def apply(mutant: Mutant, original: str) -> str:\n502|    patched = original.replace(mutant.find, mutant.replace)\n503|    if mutant.find2:\n504|        patched = patched.replace(mutant.find2, mutant.replace2)\n505|    return patched\n506|\n507|\n508|def run_mutant(mutant: Mutant) -> str:\n509|    target = REPO / mutant.path\n510|    original = target.read_text()\n511|    found = original.count(mutant.find)\n512|    if found != mutant.count:\n513|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: patch anchors {found}, want {mutant.count}\"\n514|    if mutant.find2:\n515|        found2 = original.count(mutant.find2)\n516|        if found2 != mutant.count2:\n517|            return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: second anchors {found2}, want {mutant.count2}\"\n518|    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as staging:\n519|        backup = Path(staging) / \"backup\"\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
