t reddens alone (isolated attribution from single-test runs), because each verdict lands at the release instead of the bound.\\\",\\n3021-    ),\\n3022-    Mutant(\\n3023-        name=\\\"C-control\\\",\\n===\\ninternal/tmuxserver/backend.go:439:// probeContext bounds one read-only probe by an absolute deadline:\\ninternal/tmuxserver/lifecycle.go:506:\\t\\treqBackend.deadline = lc.lesserDeadline(mctx, params.GracefulTimeoutMs)\\ninternal/tmuxserver/ops.go:423:\\treqBackend.deadline = deadline\\n===\\ninternal/tmuxserver/lifecycle_rev8_unix_test.go:102:func TestExecuteStopEscalatesAfterGracefulTimeoutAlone(t *testing.T) {\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1368,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 342,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
