ed past non-receipt entries: %v\", err)\n181|\t\t}\n182|\t})\n183|}\n184|\n185|// realDeadlineBody rewrites the operation deadline and the AX\n186|// authorization window of a closed body map onto the real clock: a\n187|// 200ms operation deadline with an hour-long authorization.\n188|func realDeadlineBody(object map[string]any, now time.Time, deadline time.Time) {\n189|\tcontext := object[\"context\"].(map[string]any)\n190|\tcontext[\"deadline_at\"] = formatTimestamp(deadline)\n191|\tcontext[\"authorization\"] = map[string]any{\n192|\t\t\"lease_id\":                  lxLease,\n193|\t\t\"lease_epoch\":               float64(7),\n194|\t\t\"holder_host_id\":            lxHost,\n195|\t\t\"authorization_kind\":        \"control\",\n196|\t\t\"issued_at\":                 formatTimestamp(now.Add(-time.Hour)),\n197|\t\t\"expires_at\":                formatTimestamp(now.Add(time.Hour)),\n198|\t\t\"authorization_evidence_id\": lxDigestA,\n199|\t}\n200|}\n201|\n202|// TestExecuteStopPollHonorsOperationDeadline pins the in-flight\n203|// bound on the stop close-confirm poll: with a 200ms operation\n204|// deadline, a has-session that stays blocked until the test\n205|// release a second later must conclude at the deadline — not at\n206|// the release — with the honest unknown (process_failed,\n207|// status_first, no kill, no closure), because absence is proven\n208|// only by positive observation. The release instant, not\n209|// scheduler latency, decides the verdict.\n210|func TestExecuteStopPollHonorsOperationDeadline(t *testing.T) {\n211|\tfx := newLifecycleFixture(t, fullLifecycleAdmitted())\n212|\tfx.lc.Now = time.Now\n213|\trelease := make(chan struct{})\n214|\trunner := newBlockingRunner(release).serve(\"send-keys\", \"\", \"\", 0).serve(\"kill-session\", \"\", \"\", 0).\n215|\t\thold(\"has-session\", \"\", \"\", 0)\n216|\tfx.lc.Runner = runner\n217|\tnow := time.Now().UTC()\n218|\tdeadline := now.Add(200 * time.Millisecond)\n219|\traw := lxStopBody(t, 3600000, func(o