{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cebb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":1464,"recorded_at":1780531400002923,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ca12-2fb8-7871-8b5c-cdfe8b1c7dd9"},"task_id":"01a0ca12-2fb8-7871-8b5c-cdfe8b1c7dd9","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ca12-2fb8-7871-8b5c-cdfe8b1c7dd9","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 14-30\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// Peers replays every recorded presentation-client receipt for one\n-// terminal instance except the requesting client itself: the stored\n-// peer census the attach overlap gate fails closed on. A stored peer\n-// is possibly live — receipts outlive their clients, and no\n-// liveness is decided here — so callers treat a non-empty census as\n-// possible overlap. The requesting client is excluded by identity:\n-// a retry replays its own receipt rather than adding a client.\n-//\n-// An unrecorded instance has no peers. A read or validation failure\n-// is an error, never an empty census: unknown is not a verdict.\n-// Staging entries (attach-*) and non-receipt names (anything without\n-// the .json suffix) are skipped; every other entry sits inside the\n-// receipt namespace and must read as a valid receipt file, so a\n-// directory at a receipt-shaped name is corruption and errors —\n-// never a skip, which would read a corrupt census as no peers.\n-// Every decoded receipt must name this session and instance, like\n-// Lookup. Peers arrive sorted by client ID.\n+// Peers replays every recorded presentation-client receipt for one\n+// terminal instance except the requesting client itself: the stored\n+// peer census the attach overlap gate fails closed on. A stored peer\n+// is possibly live — receipts outlive their clients, and no\n+// liveness is decided here — so callers treat a non-empty census as\n+// possible overlap. The requesting client is excluded by identity:\n+// a retry replays its own receipt rather than adding a client.\n+//\n+// An unrecorded instance has no peers. A read or validation failure\n+// is an error, never an empty census: unknown is not a verdict.\n+// Staging entries (attach-*) and non-receipt names (anything without\n+// the .json suffix) are skipped; every other entry sits inside the\n+// receipt namespace and admits only as a valid peer receipt for its\n+// own durable key. The admission is positive, through the keyed-read\n+// owner: the filename stem must parse as a client identity and the\n+// Lookup of that key must return the receipt. Anything else in the\n+// receipt namespace — a directory at a receipt-shaped name, valid\n+// bytes filed under another client's name, an unparseable stem —\n+// is corruption and errors, never a skip, which would read a\n+// corrupt census as no peers. Every decoded receipt must name this\n+// session and instance, like Lookup. Peers arrive sorted by client\n+// ID.\n","final_result":true}}}
