ts.\\n- STATUS: ready for review; worktree intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot. Results standalone + matrix + `TASK-260830-1c28dz_rework-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` attached to the board item.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev4 — rev3 CHANGES REQUESTED repaired on checkpoint d4bd91d\\n- SCOPE: second leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i, tmux lifecycle operations. All three P1 + P2-A + P2-B + the four surviving narrowings plus the SPW custody fifth closed in `internal/tmuxserver`; trunk unmoved, no rebase. Only touched landed files: error-code registry (new codes), ownership seam (test hook), mutant harnesses (new rows). Production `.go` delta is purely additive (0 deleted lines); all other production files are new.\\n- P1-A: quiesce/boundary barrier writes fail closed (`terminal_backend_integrity_failure` at `quiesce/boundary state image`); the outcome report commits first so retries replay the original closure time and heal the memory; attach recovers the barrier from completed closure outcomes when memory is missing (corrupt scan and empty time error). Five committed tests, seven narrowing rows.\\n- P1-B: the executed backend restore binds to the decided winner — carried `(lease_id, lease_epoch)` must equal the ordered winner or the entry refuses `local_precondition_failed` at `wrapper restore winner binding` before any effect. Three committed tests (joint + per-arm), two narrowing rows.\\n- P1-C: the refresh bound is enforced, not cooperative — the adapter runs on its own goroutine, the entry takes answer-or-deadline, late answers never verify (nil-error included), with a hook-stalled both-ready race test forcing the window deterministically. Two committed tests plus the reworked bound subtest (shared-var race removed, elapsed tightened 5s→1s), two narrowing rows. Bound B37 states the missing production mesh transport.\\n- R1-R5: exit-1 attached, foreign attached row, exit-2 panes, NUL argv, spawner root custody — five committed clause witnesses plus five