{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ece7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ca08-6c63-7352-b762-5bc242c771c8"},"sequence":5326,"recorded_at":1780531400010647,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cd8feb9b-6d69-49ce-a85c-818ca818e251"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Ready for review — TASK-260830-1c28dz handed off to review (status `to-review`), candidate left UNCOMMITTED on the Story branch at checkpoint `d4bd91d0` (50 intended paths, no commits).\n\nAll three verdict-rev9 findings closed:\n\n- **P1 — peer census whitelist.** `Peers` ([overlap.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree/internal/termbind/overlap.go)) now admits a receipt-namespace entry only as a valid peer receipt for its own durable key: the filename stem must parse as a client identity and the keyed `Lookup` of that stem must return the receipt, before the requesting-client exclusion applies. Session/instance checks, staging/non-receipt rules, and the directory refusal retained. Entry test asserts the keyed-binding refusal with no receipt, no argv, no input authorization; two narrowing rows (termbind + cross-package tmuxserver mirror), both KILLED.\n- **P2-A — escalation budget split.** Graceful wait vs post-escalation observation are distinct: pre-kill poll keeps the graceful lesser-bound, post-kill re-confirmation observes under the operation deadline via `escalationDeadline` ([backend.go](/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree/internal/tmuxserver/backend.go)). Fresh rechecks kept; timeout still unknown. New context-honoring escalation success witness + `N-stop-escalation-budget` narrowing KILLED; census gains the `escalationbound` row.\n- **P2-B — outcome corpus restored.** Rev5 driver restored byte-identically (`main.go`/`extra_off.go` unchanged; base output byte-identical to the rev5 base run), extended with `DirectivesFor` (11 keys) and `Peers` (4 keys) as declared candidate-only keys: **193 shared keys, 0 moved, 0 base-only, 22 declared candidate-only** over the complete agreed 36-package closure (33 driven + 3 stated bounds). Suite grid kept as supplementary only (2894 shared, 0 moved, 319 candidate-only all PASS in the leaf packages).\n\nVerification, all firsthand: 30/30 configured validation commands green (suite 248s, race 443s, cover 89.0%/83.5%, 17 fuzz gates); `GOOS=windows` vet with test files; changed-package race; restricted-PATH no-tmux suite (tmux unresolvable, pgrep clean, 461 PASS); harness 298/298 tmuxserver + 43/43 termbind on two full passes with per-plant raw logs; isolated shared-plant attribution 24 kills + 2 companion greens × 2 rounds on the rev10 tree; census recomputed by script (267/5536, Tables B/D byte-identical to TRACEABILITY). Matrix, results, and evidence tarball (`2ed1f346…`, 657 entries, 648/648 manifest-verified) attached and read back digest-verified.\n\nOne harness anomaly noted in LOGBOOK/results (not product, not in scope): the landed dial test relies on macOS TMPDIR paths exceeding the sun_path limit and fails in a TMPDIR-less env; the no-tmux proof runs with TMPDIR set.","reason":null}}
